  "steps": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large saucepan over medium heat. Add the onion, carrot and celery with a pinch of salt, then cook for 6 to 8 minutes until softened.",
    "Stir in the garlic and mushrooms, and cook for 8 to 10 minutes until the mushrooms have released their liquid and started to brown.",
    "Add the tomato paste, thyme and bay leaf, then cook for 1 minute to deepen the flavour.",
    "Pour in the red wine and let it bubble for 2 to 3 minutes, scraping up any browned bits from the pan.",
    "Add the lentils, canned tomatoes and water. Bring to a simmer, then reduce the heat and cook uncovered for 25 to 30 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the lentils are tender and the stew is thick.",
    "Season with salt and black pepper to taste. Remove the bay leaf, stir through the parsley, and serve hot."
